{
 "manufacturer": "Eastron",
 "model": "SDM630-Modbus",
 "short_model": "SDM630-Modbus",
 "aliases": [
  "SDM630Modbus",
  "SDM630 Modbus V2",
  "SDM630-Modbus V2"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
 "applies_to": "Eastron SDM630Modbus three-phase DIN-rail meter, protocol implementation V1.8 as published by Eastron Europe.",
 "summary": "The SDM630-Modbus is a three-phase, multifunction DIN-rail kWh meter with an RS485 Modbus RTU port. Every reading and every setting is a 32-bit IEEE-754 float spread over two registers. Measurements are input registers (function 04), configuration is in holding registers (function 03 to read, 16 to write). This map covers per-phase and system electrical values, THD, demand and per-phase import/export energy plus the communication and pulse settings.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The tables print 30001/40001-style register numbers next to the hex start address that goes on the wire; the two always differ by 30001 or 40001 (e.g. 30007 = 0x0006, which matches the document's example of reading Amps 1 at start address 0006). The reset register is printed 461457 with hex F010."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Eastron SDM630Modbus Smart Meter Modbus Protocol Implementation V1.8",
  "doc_number": "V1.8",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.eastroneurope.com/images/uploads/products/protocol/SDM630_MODBUS_Protocol.pdf",
  "pages": "Sections 1.2.1 and 1.3.1, PDF pp. 2-7"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Word order: the document states floats are sent most significant register first by default, and its read example returns 43 66 33 34 for 230.2 V. All values here are ABCD. A 'Register Order' holding register can reverse this, but the document gives no address for it, so it is not listed.",
  "Each input value is valid only for some wiring systems; values marked unavailable for the configured system read zero. The per-register descriptions say which systems return 0.",
  "Left out: 30087 'Maximum total system power demand', because the table gives its unit as VA while the matching demand register is in W.",
  "Left out: the serial number (464513), an unsigned 32-bit integer whose word order the document does not state.",
  "Read and write in register pairs: start on an even address and request an even number of registers; odd counts return an exception (a single-register read is instead answered with an instrument-type value). At most 40 values (80 registers) per request.",
  "Total kWh/kVArh registers (30343, 30345 and the per-phase totals) equal import plus export, per the source note."
 ],
